WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:17.176
Daisy Kaleem discussed the case as they headed home.

2
00:00:17.196 --> 00:00:21.877
"We already talked to all the animals in the neighborhood," Daisy said.

3
00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:23.578
"What else can we do?"

4
00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:28.779
"You didn't talk to all the animals," Beatrice said.

5
00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:31.500
"Wild animals are everywhere, you know.

6
00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:34.549
Even in neighborhoods like this."

7
00:00:34.569 --> 00:00:36.430
"Good point."

8
00:00:37.191 --> 00:00:39.412
Daisy told Kaleem what Beatrice had said.

9
00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:45.075
"Maybe a bird or squirrel saw what happened to those missing toys," she added.

10
00:00:45.095 --> 00:00:49.217
"Maybe a bird or squirrel stole them," Kaleem said.

11
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:53.600
"My mom says crows steal plant labels from her garden sometimes."

12
00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:58.563
"Raccoons steal food out of the trash," Daisy said.

13
00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:00.924
Just then she spotted a blue jay.

14
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.201
She asked him if he'd seen the missing toys.

15
00:01:04.221 --> 00:01:07.382
"Are you accusing me of something?"

16
00:01:07.762 --> 00:01:08.482
he demanded.

17
00:01:08.502 --> 00:01:11.103
"No," Daisy said.

18
00:01:11.123 --> 00:01:15.404
"Er, unless you're the one who took those toys?"

19
00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:17.925
"Absolutely not!"

20
00:01:19.365 --> 00:01:20.245
the jay huffed.

21
00:01:20.645 --> 00:01:21.726
Then he cocked his head.

22
00:01:21.746 --> 00:01:26.667
"Although I heard there was a raccoon wandering around last night.

23
00:01:27.327 --> 00:01:30.048
Everyone knows raccoons are thieves."

24
00:01:30.796 --> 00:01:33.017
Daisy told Kaleem what the jay had said.

25
00:01:33.037 --> 00:01:37.018
"Let's go into the forest," Kaleem said.

26
00:01:37.038 --> 00:01:39.059
"We might find a raccoon there."

27
00:01:45.641 --> 00:01:48.502
In the forest Daisy talked to a few animals.

28
00:01:50.522 --> 00:01:53.303
But none of them had seen any raccoons lately.

29
00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:00.885
Finally she asked a chipmunk.

30
00:02:01.745 --> 00:02:05.947
"There's a raccoon sleeping in this tree right now," the chipmunk said.

31
00:02:05.967 --> 00:02:12.389
"Thanks." As the chipmunk skittered off, Daisy called to the raccoon.

32
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:17.291
A masked face peeked out of a hole in the tree trunk.

33
00:02:17.311 --> 00:02:19.652
"Who are you?"

34
00:02:20.153 --> 00:02:22.153
the raccoon asked sleepily.

35
00:02:22.173 --> 00:02:25.235
"Why are you waking me up?"

36
00:02:25.955 --> 00:02:28.016
Daisy explained about the missing toys.

37
00:02:29.992 --> 00:02:33.714
"I don't want to accuse you of anything," she said politely.

38
00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:38.896
"But I've heard that raccoons sometimes, um, borrow stuff."

39
00:02:40.596 --> 00:02:46.179
"I won't deny it," the raccoon said with a yawn.

40
00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.860
"But I have no interest in toys.

41
00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:54.622
And while I wouldn't say no to a nice bone, I haven't taken any lately."

42
00:02:54.642 --> 00:02:58.964
"Human girl," a voice said.

43
00:02:59.644 --> 00:03:01.405
"I know where you should look."

44
00:03:01.425 --> 00:03:02.265
Daisy turned.

45
00:03:04.226 --> 00:03:06.728
A doe was peering out of some underbrush.

46
00:03:06.748 --> 00:03:13.011
"Follow this trail to the sunny clearing," the deer said before bounding away.

47
00:03:21.795 --> 00:03:27.030
When Daisy and Kaleem reached the clearing, two foxes were sitting on a rock.

48
00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:31.875
They were watching their young cubs play with "Pet toys!"

49
00:03:32.275 --> 00:03:33.096
Daisy cried.

50
00:03:33.116 --> 00:03:34.937
"Hide, children!"

51
00:03:35.278 --> 00:03:36.138
the mother barked.

52
00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:40.542
"You don't have to hide," Daisy called.

53
00:03:40.562 --> 00:03:43.605
"We won't hurt you."

54
00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:46.608
"You can understand what we say?"

55
00:03:47.128 --> 00:03:48.149
the father asked.

56
00:03:48.169 --> 00:03:51.072
"Yes," Daisy said.

57
00:03:52.308 --> 00:03:55.130
"And now I understand why you took those pet toys.

58
00:03:56.612 --> 00:03:58.353
But they belong to other animals.

59
00:03:58.974 --> 00:04:00.795
And those animals miss their toys."

60
00:04:00.815 --> 00:04:05.139
"Our cubs need to play," the mother said.

61
00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:10.683
Daisy touched her pocket, which held the money from Finn's owner.

62
00:04:10.703 --> 00:04:13.586
"I know!

63
00:04:14.046 --> 00:04:17.429
I'll go to the pet store right now and buy your cubs some toys.

64
00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.872
After that, can I return these toys?"

65
00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:26.532
The foxes agreed, and Daisy explained everything to Kaleem.

66
00:04:26.552 --> 00:04:32.318
"Finn and the others will be so happy," he said.

67
00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:35.722
"The cubs will be happy too."

68
00:04:36.363 --> 00:04:37.324
Daisy smiled.

69
00:04:37.344 --> 00:04:39.486
"You know what, Kaleem?

70
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:42.829
It feels great to help all kinds of animals!"
